    <string name="privacy_text">Redes has no ads or analytics. It reads what Android says about your connection and the Wi‑Fi networks nearby; the location or nearby devices permissions only serve to see network names: it never reads or keeps where you are. The speed test downloads and uploads filler data with Cloudflare\'s public server (speed.cloudflare.com); nothing of yours is sent. Tests are kept only on this phone, out of cloud backups. Only if you turn on MCP mode, the AI you connect with a token can see your connection and tests and, with a read-and-write token, start a test, through the relay.</string>
